# Reference Intelligence Engine (RIE)

Phase: 154 (adopted 2026-09-14)
Owns: references/engine.sdd
Principle: the AI does not copy — it extracts DECISIONS from
references. (No cloning: extract decisions, never assets/code/markup.)

## Pipeline

```
INPUT (URLs / Docs / Images / Repos)
  -> CRAWL (fetch, render, relevant pages)
  -> EXTRACT (visual/structural/pattern elements)
  -> ANALYZE (understand + classify)
  -> COMPARE (multi-reference: COMMON/UNIQUE/STRONG/WEAK/CONFLICT)
  -> DISTILL (design language, not code: density/tone/spacing/
     typography/navigation/interaction)
  -> ADAPT (Project Fit: constraints vs reference -> FIT ANALYSIS)
  -> VALIDATE (evidence levels: OBSERVED -> INFERRED -> VALIDATED
     -> ADOPTED -> STANDARD)
  -> ADOPT (TAKE / ADAPT / REJECT / IGNORE per pattern, with reason)
  -> LINK INTO SDD (patterns.sdd, decisions.sdd, skill updates)
```

## Reference Contract (.reference object)

```
id: REF-<n>
source: {type: web|doc|image|repo, url}
intent: INSPIRE | CLONE-forbidden-but-study | COMPARE | STUDY |
  DOCUMENT | IMPLEMENT | RESEARCH | COMPETITOR |
  API_REFERENCE | ARCHITECTURE_REFERENCE
scope: [visual, ux, interaction, architecture, api, security,
  performance, devops, business-flow]
forbid: [direct-copy, source-assets, code-transfer]
target: @project.<area>
```

Intent default: INSPIRE when user gives bare URLs + a goal.

## Scope prioritization

User emphasis decides depth: "I like this dashboard design"
(translated from the customer's Azerbaijani prompt — the raw
wording is preserved in the prompt-pair ledger [R104])
-> homepage/dashboard/navigation/cards/tables/forms/responsive = high;
blog/legal/footer/irrelevant = low. Crawl relevant pages only.

## Multi-Reference Matrix

| Area | Ref A | Ref B | Ref C | Decision |
|------|-------|-------|-------|----------|
| Navigation | rating | rating | rating | winner + why |

Ratings derive from extracted evidence, not taste. Conflicts
(STRONG vs STRONG) route to DEC with the matrix attached.

## Project Fit Analysis

Reference pattern vs project constraints (type: enterprise/banking/
small VPS; scale L0-L5; audience) -> FIT | ADAPT | REJECT with
reason. Example: huge hero + B2B admin panel = REJECT (page intent
mismatch). Excessive animation + enterprise banking = REDUCE.

## Decision record (per pattern)

```
pattern: <name>
decision: TAKE | ADAPT | REJECT | IGNORE
reason: [evidence bullets]
source: REF-<n>
```

## Skill linkage

3 references + same interaction pattern + project need
-> check existing skill FIRST ([SK13]):
- exists -> add REF-<n> as evidence to @skill.<name> (link, no copy)
- new domain -> SKILL_EVOLUTION record (child of parent skill where
  applicable; see skills/evolution.sdd Phase 136)
- never create duplicate skills — deduplication runs before creation

## Evidence levels

OBSERVED -> INFERRED -> VALIDATED -> ADOPTED -> STANDARD
(evidence: N references; confidence: high/medium/low; validated:
yes/no; adopted: project-only | shared)

## Ingestion & provenance ([R110] [R111])

URL -> tmp/ RAW SNAPSHOT (html/css/screenshots, ephemeral)
-> ANALYSIS -> EXTRACT KNOWLEDGE -> PROVENANCE RECORD
-> DELETE TMP ([R96] tmp rule).

Provenance survives deletion:
```
source: <url>
captured: <date>
evidence: design observation | architecture analysis | ...
derived: @pattern.<name>
```

## Reference storage

.sdd/references/
  INDEX.sdd            routing
  web/REF-<n>.sdd      one per analyzed reference (contract + observed
                       + extracted + adopted + rejected + confidence)
  design/patterns.sdd  distilled patterns
  design/decisions.sdd reference-driven design decisions
Project research cases: .sdd/projects/<name>/research/DR-<n>.sdd
  (goal, references, findings w/ source, decision; re-runnable —
  @research DR-<n> reuses results; REFRESH_STATUS fresh|stale|
  changed|unavailable triggers re-analysis on demand)

## Reference Delta & Freshness

REF-<n>.last_checked + source_changed detection:
- source changed -> REF DELTA reported; adopted patterns keep
  (SOURCE_CHANGED, PROJECT_RULE_UNCHANGED) — reference is never
  automatic authority over project rules ([R110]).
- unavailable -> mark stale, keep provenance.

## Vocabulary

@ref (the reference object) | @inspiration (intent) |
@pattern (distilled pattern) | @design (design language) |
@research (DR case) | @benchmark (comparison set)

## Applicability

Same engine, all domains: DESIGN, UX, ARCHITECTURE, API, SECURITY,
PERFORMANCE, DEVOPS, CODE PATTERN, BUSINESS FLOW. Flow is identical;
scope/intent/forbid differ.

State: +
